ded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIyMDAiIGhlaWdodD0iMTI5IiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMjAwIDEyOSI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"129\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/610819_08-200x129.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"The Beatles at Aintree Institute, Liverpool, 19 August 1961\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/610819_08-200x129.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/610819_08-580x373.jpg 580w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/610819_08.jpg 747w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"12761\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1961-photos/610819_08/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/610819_08.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"747,481\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"The Beatles at Aintree Institute, Liverpool, 19 August 1961\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/610819_08.jpg\"></a></div></figure><figure class=\"gallery-item\"><div class=\"gallery-icon landscape\">\n<a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1961-photos/610819_09/\"><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIyMDAiIGhlaWdodD0iMTMzIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMjAwIDEzMyI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"133\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/610819_09-200x133.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"Paul McCartney and the Shimmy-Shimmy Queens at Aintree Institute, Liverpool, 19 August 1961\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/610819_09-200x133.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/610819_09-580x385.jpg 580w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/610819_09.jpg 760w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"12762\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1961-photos/610819_09/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/610819_09.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"760,505\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"Paul McCartney and the Shimmy-Shimmy Queens at Aintree Institute, Liverpool, 19 August 1961\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/610819_09.jpg\"></a></div></figure></div><p>The Beatles played at Aintree Institute on 31 occasions, between this date and January 1962. The other dates were <a href=\"/1961/01/07/live-aintree-institute-liverpool/\">7</a>, <a href=\"/1961/01/13/live-aintree-institute-liverpool-2/\">13</a>, <a href=\"/1961/01/14/live-aintree-institute-liverpool-3/\">14</a>, <a href=\"/1961/01/18/live-aintree-institute-liverpool-4/\">18</a>, <a href=\"/1961/01/21/live-aintree-institute-liverpool-5/\">21</a>, <a href=\"/1961/01/27/live-aintree-institute-liverpool-6/\">27</a> and <a href=\"/1961/01/28/live-aintree-institute-liverpool-7/\">28 January</a>; <a href=\"/1961/02/08/live-aintree-institute-liverpool-8/\">8</a>, <a href=\"/1961/02/10/live-aintree-institute-liverpool-9/\">10</a>, <a href=\"/1961/02/15/live-aintree-institute-liverpool-10/\">15</a>, <a href=\"/1961/02/18/live-aintree-institute-liverpool-11/\">18</a>, <a href=\"/1961/02/22/live-aintree-institute-liverpool-12/\">22</a> and <a href=\"/1961/02/25/live-aintree-institute-liverpool-13/\">25 February</a>; <a href=\"/1961/03/01/live-aintree-institute-liverpool-14/\">1</a>, <a href=\"/1961/03/04/live-aintree-institute-liverpool-15/\">4</a>, <a href=\"/1961/03/08/live-aintree-institute-liverpool-16/\">8</a> and <a href=\"/1961/03/11/live-aintree-institute-liverpool-17/\">11 March</a>; <a href=\"/1961/07/21/live-aintree-institute-liverpool-18/\">21</a> and <a href=\"/1961/07/28/live-aintree-institute-liverpool-19/\">28 July</a>; <a href=\"/1961/08/04/live-aintree-institute-liverpool-20/\">4</a>, <a href=\"/1961/08/12/live-aintree-institute-liverpool-21/\">12</a>, <a href=\"/1961/08/18/live-aintree-institute-liverpool-22/\">18</a> and <a href=\"/1961/08/26/live-aintree-institute-liverpool-24/\">26 August</a>; <a href=\"/1961/09/02/live-aintree-institute-liverpool-25/\">2</a>, <a href=\"/1961/09/09/live-aintree-institute-liverpool-26/\">9</a>, <a href=\"/1961/09/16/live-aintree-institute-liverpool-27/\">16</a> and <a href=\"/1961/09/23/live-aintree-institute-liverpool-28/\">23 September</a>; <a href=\"/1961/10/28/live-aintree-institute-liverpool-29/\">28 October</a>; <a href=\"/1961/11/11/live-aintree-institute-liverpool-30/\">11 November 1961</a>; and <a href=\"/1962/01/27/live-aintree-institute-liverpool-31/\">27 January 1962</a>.</p><p>Aintree Institute was a popular jive club in the early 1960s. It was situated behind the Black Bull club, near to the famous racecourse where the annual Grand National horse race takes place, but was demolished in 2007.</p>\n<!--[googlesitekit-end-of-content]--><div style=\"font-size: 12px; margin: 10px 0 10px 0;\"><strong>Page last updated:</strong> 24 January 2024</div></div></div><div class=\"on-this-day-wrapper\"><h3>Also on this day...</h3><ul><li>2010: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/2010/08/19/paul-mccartney-live-consol-energy-center-pittsburgh-2/\">Paul McCartney live: Consol Energy Center, Pittsburgh</a></li><li>2009: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/2009/08/19/paul-mccartney-live-cowboys-stadium-dallas/\">Paul McCartney live: Cowboys Stadium, Dallas</a></li><li>2003: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/2003/08/19/ringo-starr-all-starr-band-live-alico-arena-fort-myers/\">Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Alico Arena, Fort Myers</a></li><li>2001: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/2001/08/19/ringo-starr-all-starr-band-live-frontier-city-oklahoma-city/\">Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Frontier City, Oklahoma City</a></li><li>1995: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1995/08/19/ringo-starr-all-starr-band-live-greek-theatre-los-angeles-6/\">Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Greek Theatre, Los Angeles</a></li><li>1989: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1989/08/19/ringo-starr-all-starr-band-live-cne-grandstand-toronto/\">Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: CNE Grandstand, Toronto</a></li><li>1980: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1980/08/19/recording-every-man-has-a-woman-who-loves-him-hard-times-are-over-john-lennon-yoko-ono/\">Recording: Every Man Has A Woman Who Loves Him, Hard Times Are Over by John Lennon and Yoko Ono</a></li><li>1972: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1972/08/19/wings-live-martinihal-groningen/\">Wings live: Martinihal, Groningen</a></li><li>1971: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1971/08/19/recording-blindman-ringo-starr-2/\">Recording: Blindman by Ringo Starr</a></li><li>1969: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1969/08/19/recording-mixing-the-end-golden-slumbers-carry-that-weight-something-here-comes-the-sun/\">Recording, mixing: The End, Golden Slumbers, Carry That Weight, Something, Here Comes The Sun</a></li><li>1967: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1967/08/19/jason-starkey-is-born/\">Jason Starkey is born</a></li><li>1966: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1966/08/19/live-mid-south-coliseum-memphis/\">The Beatles live: Mid-South Coliseum, Memphis</a></li><li>1965: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1965/08/19/live-sam-houston-coliseum-houston/\">The Beatles live: Sam Houston Coliseum, Houston</a></li><li>1964: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1964/08/19/live-cow-palace-san-francisco/\">The Beatles live: Cow Palace, San Francisco</a></li><li>1963: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1963/08/19/live-gaumont-cinema-bournemouth/\">The Beatles live: Gaumont Cinema, Bournemouth</a></li><li>1962: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1962/08/19/live-cavern-club-liverpool-217/\">The Beatles live: Cavern Club, Liverpool (evening)</a></li><li>1960: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1960/08/19/live-indra-club-hamburg-3/\">The Beatles live: Indra Club, Hamburg</a></li></ul><p>Want more? Visit the <a title=\"Day after day: the Beatles' history\" href=\"/history/\">Beatles history section</a>.</p></div><div class=\"gm-map\" style=\"position: relative;height: 390px; width: 100%;\"><iframe data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"about:blank\" name=\"gm-map-1\" allowfullscreen=\"\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/?geo_mashup_content=render-map&amp;map_data_key=45bc4475ddf0db3197cc0f3a402a1e7e&amp;height=390&amp;width=100%&amp;add_overview_control=false&amp;zoom=16&amp;enable_street_view=false&amp;map_type=G_HYBRID_MAP&amp;name=gm-map-1&amp;object_id=12681&amp;map_content=single\" style=\"position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border: none; overflow: hidden;\" title=\"Geo Mashup Map\"></iframe></div>",
  "textContent": "This was the 23rd performance given by The Beatles at Aintree Institute, which was situated at Longmoor Lane in Aintree, Liverpool. It was put on by Brian Kelly, who ran Beekay Promotions in Liverpool, and was the second of seven consecutive Saturday night bookings for The Beatles at the venue.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe Beatles played at Aintree Institute on 31 occasions, between this date and January 1962. The other dates were 7, 13, 14, 18, 21, 27 and 28 January; 8, 10, 15, 18, 22 and 25 February; 1, 4, 8 and 11 March; 21 and 28 July; 4, 12, 18 and 26 August; 2, 9, 16 and 23 September; 28 October; 11 November 1961; and 27 January 1962.Aintree Institute was a popular jive club in the early 1960s. It was situated behind the Black Bull club, near to the famous racecourse where the annual Grand National horse race takes place, but was demolished in 2007.\nPage last updated: 24 January 2024Also on this day...2010: Paul McCartney live: Consol Energy Center, Pittsburgh2009: Paul McCartney live: Cowboys Stadium, Dallas2003: Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Alico Arena, Fort Myers2001: Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Frontier City, Oklahoma City1995: Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Greek Theatre, Los Angeles1989: Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: CNE Grandstand, Toronto1980: Recording: Every Man Has A Woman Who Loves Him, Hard Times Are Over by John Lennon and Yoko Ono1972: Wings live: Martinihal, Groningen1971: Recording: Blindman by Ringo Starr1969: Recording, mixing: The End, Golden Slumbers, Carry That Weight, Something, Here Comes The Sun1967: Jason Starkey is born1966: The Beatles live: Mid-South Coliseum, Memphis1965: The Beatles live: Sam Houston Coliseum, Houston1964: The Beatles live: Cow Palace, San Francisco1963: The Beatles live: Gaumont Cinema, Bournemouth1962: The Beatles live: Cavern Club, Liverpool (evening)1960: The Beatles live: Indra Club, HamburgWant more? Visit the Beatles history section.",
